bbaddepudi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbaddepudi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-03-22T23:09:01Z","updated_at":"2018-03-22T23:09:01Z","body":"Few observations:\r\n- Replica C gets tombstones the tablet incorrectly after a remote bootstrap (RBS) which was fine otherwise.\r\n- The RBS does go ahead and issue a CHANGE_ROLE, but replica C does not get to process that consensus update.\r\n- So other replicas A & B believe C is part of the quorum as a VOTER, as they do apply the CHANGE_ROLE.\r\n\r\nThe ideal case (as was before) is to keep C in the quorum even if it does not apply the CHANGE_ROLE immediately after an otherwise successful RBS. That way it would eventually apply the change role, become a voter and help A win the election...\r\n\r\n @hectorgcr is digging into the resolution to revert a possible regression and fix it up.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/375486984/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bbaddepudi","id":6334739,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMzQ3Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6334739?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bb